From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:16:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): rewrite the settings UI in Jetpack Compose
 (Material 3 Expressive)

Replace the AndroidX-Preference settings host with a Compose activity and
migrate the pages to Jetpack Compose, keeping the input view untouched.

- MainActivity is now a ComponentActivity hosting SettingsApp with
  MaterialExpressiveTheme; the previous implementation is preserved as
  NativeSettingsActivity and stays reachable for pages not migrated yet
  (openNative fallback), so deep links and ACTION_VIEW/RUN flows keep working.
- Compose pages: home (sections + real typing heatmap card with a day
  tooltip), Fcitx RawConfig screens (global / addon / input method), managed
  preference screens (keyboard, candidates, clipboard, symbols, advanced),
  input method & addon lists, about / licenses / plugins / developer, and the
  statistics & heatmap settings page (palette sheet, custom colour via the
  existing picker, tracking switch, reset).
- HeatmapCard renders the real TypingStatsManager snapshot: 53-week grid,
  palette preferences observed live, day tooltip with a notch that tracks the
  tapped cell and a bubble clamped inside the heatmap bounds.
- Raise compileSdk to 37 and minSdk to 24 (required by Compose 1.12 /
  material3 1.5), enable the Compose compiler, add the Compose BOM 2026.09.00
  plus activity-compose / lifecycle-compose / material-icons-extended.
- Add a self-contained androidTest resource overlay so instrumented test APKs
  link again after the resValue propagation change, and update
  ThemeSerializationTest for theme version 2.1 (upstream 888289da).
- Document the migration status in docs/settings-compose-migration.md.
