diff --git a/docs/settings-compose-migration.md b/docs/settings-compose-migration.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5d860093
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/settings-compose-migration.md
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+# Settings UI migration progress
+
+Settings (`MainActivity`) is now a **Jetpack Compose** host using **Material 3 Expressive**
+(`material3 1.5.0-rc01`, `MaterialExpressiveTheme` + expressive motion scheme). The previous
+AndroidX-Preference implementation is preserved as `NativeSettingsActivity` and stays reachable
+as a fallback for destinations that are not migrated yet.
+
+The input view (keyboard, candidate bar, popups) is untouched.
+
+## Status (2026-11-15)
+
+| Destination | Route | State |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Home (heatmap hero + sections) | `home` | ✅ Compose (`compose/home/HomeScreen.kt` + `home/HeatmapCard.kt`); heatmap renders the real `TypingStatsManager` snapshot (53-week grid, palette prefs live, day tooltip) |
+| Global options (RawConfig) | `global` | ✅ Compose (`screens/RawConfig.kt`, `RawConfigControls.kt`) |
+| Addon config (RawConfig) | `addon/<uniqueName>` | ✅ Compose, incl. the `table` synthetic `AndroidTable` row |
+| Input method config (RawConfig) | `im/<uniqueName>` | ✅ Compose |
+| Input method list | `im_list` | ✅ Compose (`screens/DataScreens.kt`), enable/order persists via `setEnabledIme` (+ subtype sync on API 34+) |
+| Addon list | `addon_list` | ✅ Compose, grouped by `AddonCategory`, toggle persists via `setAddonState` |
+| Virtual keyboard | `virtual_keyboard` | ✅ Compose (`screens/Preferences.kt`, `PreferenceControls.kt`), renders `ManagedPreferenceUi` without inflating AndroidX views |
+| Candidates | `candidates` | ✅ Compose (same mechanism) |
+| Clipboard | `clipboard` | ✅ Compose (same mechanism) |
+| Emoji & symbols | `symbol` | ✅ Compose (same mechanism) |
+| Advanced | `advanced` | ✅ Compose (same mechanism) |
+| About | `about` | ✅ Compose (version, links, build info, credits) |
+| Licenses | `license` | ✅ Compose via AboutLibraries (`R.raw.aboutlibraries`) |
+| Plugins | `plugin` | ✅ Compose (loaded/failed plugins, plugin-change detection, `FcitxDaemon.restartFcitx`) |
+| Developer | `developer` | ✅ Compose (logs, verbose log, inspector, restart, delete-and-sync, heap dump) |
+| Theme editor | `theme` | ⏳ legacy (`openNative`) |
+| Typing stats detail | `stats` | ✅ Compose (`screens/StatsScreen.kt`): palette sheet with per-option previews, custom color (reuses the legacy `HeatmapColorPickerDialog`), tracking switch via `TypingStatsManager.setEnabled`, reset with confirm dialog. The home heatmap card is `home/HeatmapCard.kt` |
+| File manager | `files` | ⏳ legacy (`openNative`) |
+| Quick phrase / punctuation / table IM / pinyin dict editors | — | ⏳ legacy (reachable from RawConfig external actions) |
+
+## Architecture
+
+- `MainActivity` : `ComponentActivity`, `enableEdgeToEdge()`, `setContent { FcitxSettingsTheme { SettingsApp(...) } }`.
+- `SettingsApp` owns a lightweight `SettingsNavigator` (route stack + `BackHandler`); each
+  destination is a function of the route string. No navigation-library dependency.
+- `SettingsViewModel` holds the settings-scoped `FcitxConnection` (`FcitxDaemon.connect`) used by
+  RawConfig/IM/addon pages; saved state is flushed in `onStop` (`fcitx.runIfReady { save() }`).
+- RawConfig pages parse `ConfigDescriptor.parseTopLevel(raw["desc"])` exactly like
+  `PreferenceScreenFactory` and write through `setGlobalConfig` / `setAddonConfig` / `setImConfig`;
+  saves are coalesced and serialized by a Mutex with rollback to the last good snapshot.
+- ManagedPreference pages read `provider.managedPreferencesUi` / `managedPreferences` and write
+  through `ManagedPreference.setValue` + `provider.fireChange(key)`, so dependent rows
+  (`enableUiOn`) enable/disable live.
+- Unmigrated destinations open `NativeSettingsActivity` (registered in the manifest, still on
+  `Theme.FcitxAppTheme.Md3`) with the original `SettingsRoute` extras; deep links
+  (`ACTION_RUN`, dictionary import `ACTION_VIEW`, setup flow, notification/storage permission
+  prompts) keep working unchanged.
+
+## Build knobs
+
+- `compileSdk = 37`, `minSdk = 24` (Compose 1.12 / material3 1.5 require API 37 metadata and
+  minSdk 24; the Flutter attempt raised these first and they stay).
+- Compose is enabled app-wide: `kotlin-compose` plugin + BOM `2026.09.00` +
+  `material3 1.5.0-rc01` (expressive APIs), `material-icons-extended`, `activity-compose`,
+  `lifecycle-runtime/viewmodel-compose`.
+- Build: `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug`. Toolchain env used in this workspace:
+  `ANDROID_HOME=…/.toolchain/android-sdk ANDROID_USER_HOME=…/.toolchain/android-home
+  HOME=…/.toolchain/home GRADLE_USER_HOME=…/.toolchain/gradle-home`.
+
+## Tests
+
+- `:app:testDebugUnitTest` — **69/69 pass** (5 suites). Includes `ThemeSerializationTest`,
+  which was failing on this branch before the migration (upstream fixed it in `888289da`
+  after the theme version bump to 2.1; that fix is applied here as part of the test run).
+- `:app:connectedDebugAndroidTest` — the test APK now **builds and links**. The previous
+  failure was unrelated to the Compose migration: the debug build type's `resValue`s
+  (`app_icon → @mipmap/ic_launcher_debug` etc.) propagate into the androidTest variant, whose
+  AAPT link cannot see the app's main resources. Fixed with a self-contained androidTest
+  resource overlay (`app/src/androidTest/res/`: placeholder launcher mipmaps +
+  `app_name_debug`), documented in that file.
+  Execution on the PJF110 phone (2026-11-15): APKs install and the suite launches, but
+  `FcitxTest.testWbx` was interrupted mid-run (83.6s, empty failure body, 1 of 3 tests reached,
+  instrumentation process hijacked by the app's own MainActivity/SetupActivity starting inside
+  the test process). This suite drives the C++ input engine (wubi/pinyin commit) and was written
+  for the CI emulator; on a daily-driver phone — where the engine profile is shared with the
+  installed IME and the run reinstalls/uninstalls the app — it is environment-hostile. The run
+  also always uninstalls the debug app afterwards (standard AGP behavior). Recommended: run this
+  suite on a dedicated emulator; `ANDROID_SERIAL=<serial> ./gradlew :app:connectedDebugAndroidTest`.
+
+## Verified on device (PJF110, Android 15)
+
+`assembleDebug` → install → launch: home, global options, advanced (switch + enum bottom
+sheet), input method list + Ziranma config (slider/bool/enum), addons list + Pinyin config.
+Rendering uses dynamic color (wallpaper palette) on Android 12+; no crashes in logcat.
